SUMMARY:Trail Cons. - Conversation with the Artist | Eastside Family Garden
  Project
LOCATION:Lorraine “Grandma” Camacho Activity Center\, 35 Robert T Marti
 nez Jr St\, Austin\, TX 78702
URL:https://thetrailconservancy.org/event/community-design-workshop-eastsid
 e-family-garden-project/
DESCRIPTION:Join The Trail Conservancy for a Meet the Artist event for the 
 Eastside Play Area project! Talk with the project’s artist\, Lys Santama
 ria and landscape architect\, Rialto Studio. Together\, we’ll explore ho
 w community stories and creativity can shape the art that makes our park a
  true reflection of home.\nFree Tacos and Beverages will be provided.\nGet
  to Know the Artist: Lys Santamaria\nSelected from an open call in July\, 
 Lys is a Colombian-born\, Austin-based artist whose work in glass beads an
 d tile explores joy\, healing\, and storytelling inspired by her identity 
 as a Latina\, woman\, and immigrant.\nAs a public artist\, Lys describes h
 er role as “a translator”—listening to communities\, honoring their 
 stories\, and reflecting them through intentional design. Her current proj
 ects include a commission for the Joan Means Khabele Bathhouse Rehabilitat
 ion.\nAbout the Project\n…\n\nDetails: https://thetrailconservancy.org/e
 vent/community-design-workshop-eastside-family-garden-project/
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:trailcons
END:VEVENT
