SUMMARY:Trail Cons. - Open House: Programming for the Butler Trail and Seah
 olm Waterfront
LOCATION:Seaholm Intake Facility\, 801 West Cesar Chavez Street\, Austin\, 
 TX 78701
URL:https://thetrailconservancy.org/event/open-house-seaholm-waterfront/
DESCRIPTION:New community engagement focuses exclusively on shaping future 
 public programming for the Butler Trail and the future Seaholm Waterfront\
 , and we invite community input to guide activities that are engaging\, ed
 ucational\, and uniquely Austin.\nThe Seaholm Intake Building (801 W Cesar
  Chavez St) is an iconic\, historic building set right on the Trail that o
 ffers a world of possibility. In partnership with the Austin Parks and Rec
 reation Department\, The Trail Conservancy will undertake a renovation of 
 this building and its grounds to create Seaholm Waterfront\, a unique spac
 e for everyone who lives\, works\, and travels in Austin. Phase 2 renovati
 ons could include a cafe\, overhead doors\, a front porch\, indoor restroo
 ms\, a lake overlook\, a front lawn\, seating areas\, and planting areas.\
 n…\n\nDetails: https://thetrailconservancy.org/event/open-house-seaholm-
 waterfront/
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:trailcons
